{"name":"Charolais Cattle","hex":"#f1ebea","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cattle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Domesticated animals of the species Bos taurus (cows, bulls, steers, oxen etc), and other hoofed mammals of the genus Bos.","Certain other livestock, such as sheep, pigs or goats. Also rarely applied to horses."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Ellipsis of cattle truck (“to fuck: to break, destroy”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cattle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Charolais cattle","blocks":[{"text":"The Charolais or Charolaise is a French breed of taurine beef cattle. It originates in, and is named for, the Charolais area surrounding Charolles, in the département of Saône-et-Loire in the Bourgogne-Franche-Comté region of eastern France. It is known for its colours, which can vary from white to wheaten."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Vache_de_race_charolaise_avec_son_veau.jpg/330px-Vache_de_race_charolaise_avec_son_veau.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charolais_cattle"},{"title":"Cattle","blocks":[{"text":"Cattle are large, domesticated, bovid ungulates widely kept as livestock. They are prominent modern members of the subfamily Bovinae and the most widespread species of the genus Bos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Cow_%28Fleckvieh_breed%29_Oeschinensee_Slaunger_2009-07-07.jpg/330px-Cow_%28Fleckvieh_breed%29_Oeschinensee_Slaunger_2009-07-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cattle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Taureau_charolais_-_Salon_de_l%27Agriculture_de_Paris_2010.jpg/500px-Taureau_charolais_-_Salon_de_l%27Agriculture_de_Paris_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"ht